[
    {
        "content": "<p>I tested out removing <code>#[readonly]</code> from <code>VMFuncRef</code> fields as part of <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14683\">https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14683</a> and I was surprised to see no substantive changes in the disas test suite. Everything was just loads dropping the <code>readonly</code> flag.</p>\n<p>I tried adding a test like this:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">module</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cp\">$f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">func</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">func</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">param</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cp\">$x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">ref</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cp\">$f</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">call_ref</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cp\">$f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">local</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cp\">$x</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">call_ref</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cp\">$f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">local</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cp\">$x</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>but even that compiles to:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">v3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">load</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"kt\">i64</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">user16</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">aligned</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">readonly</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">region2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v2</span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"mi\">8</span>\n<span class=\"n\">v4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">load</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"kt\">i64</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">notrap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">aligned</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">readonly</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">region3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v2</span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"mi\">24</span>\n<span class=\"n\">call_indirect</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sig0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v3</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">v4</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">v5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">load</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"kt\">i64</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">user16</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">aligned</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">readonly</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">region2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v2</span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"mi\">8</span>\n<span class=\"n\">v6</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">load</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"kt\">i64</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">notrap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">aligned</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">readonly</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">region3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v2</span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"mi\">24</span>\n<span class=\"n\">call_indirect</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sig0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v5</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">v6</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and I'm surprised by this -- is this a bug in Cranelift? <code>v5</code> is dominated by <code>v3</code> and <code>v6</code> by <code>v4</code>, so shouldn't <code>v5</code>/<code>v6</code> be eliminated loads with what's implemented in Cranelift?</p>",
        "id": 633145013,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Crichton",
        "timestamp": 1792447644
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I would expect so! I'm in transit now but can stare at this a little bit later</p>",
        "id": 633145579,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Fallin",
        "timestamp": 1792447849
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>oh apparently <code>.readonly()</code> is only read in egraphs right now and it's only used when combined with can_move/notrap to make it a pure egraph node -- which in that case I'd expect <code>v6</code> to be GVN'd... but that'd explain why <code>v5</code> isn't GVN'd</p>",
        "id": 633146838,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Crichton",
        "timestamp": 1792448213
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>hmm, semantically at least I'd expect even trappable, cannot-move loads to disappear when dominated by another identical load. I had thought the \"idempotent ops\" mechanism was built for this case but my memory is fuzzy, will have to dig more</p>",
        "id": 633147284,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Fallin",
        "timestamp": 1792448369
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>oh wait right none of these are <code>can_move</code>, ok well that explains why nothing happens today at least</p>",
        "id": 633147373,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Crichton",
        "timestamp": 1792448398
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(I guess these can't be notrap because we let a null funcref trap, right?)</p>",
        "id": 633147384,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Fallin",
        "timestamp": 1792448401
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>yeah, despite this being a non-nullable funcref...</p>",
        "id": 633147411,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Crichton",
        "timestamp": 1792448411
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(we don't plumb that much type info yet)</p>",
        "id": 633147423,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Crichton",
        "timestamp": 1792448416
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>well, the lack of <code>can_move</code> explains why egraphs don't handle this</p>",
        "id": 633147498,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Crichton",
        "timestamp": 1792448440
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>in principle I guess they should be can-move? I mean readonly implies that whenever you read the thing, it'll have the same value</p>",
        "id": 633147532,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Fallin",
        "timestamp": 1792448452
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(this is where my mental model for the semantics wants a clearer semantics)</p>",
        "id": 633147536,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Fallin",
        "timestamp": 1792448452
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>IIRC we did that historically but had to move away b/c it move above control flow saying \"ok go actually do that\"</p>",
        "id": 633147607,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Crichton",
        "timestamp": 1792448480
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>basically it was a control-flow sensitive decision to determine whether we should even do the load, but with <code>can_move</code> it moved up above the control flow</p>",
        "id": 633147668,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Crichton",
        "timestamp": 1792448504
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>hmm, ah, yeah. hoisting can move the location of the trap if there is a trap</p>",
        "id": 633147696,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Fallin",
        "timestamp": 1792448515
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>that shouldn't prevent us from GVN'ing on top of another one that is already forced though</p>",
        "id": 633147766,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Fallin",
        "timestamp": 1792448534
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>in principle at least</p>",
        "id": 633147781,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Fallin",
        "timestamp": 1792448538
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>makes sense yeah</p>",
        "id": 633147814,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Crichton",
        "timestamp": 1792448552
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>ok I'm on Portland lightrail with flaky cell right now but I'll poke at this more when I'm in my hotel, I'm now freshly annoyed by our semantics :-)</p>",
        "id": 633147916,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Fallin",
        "timestamp": 1792448586
    },
